1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,531
Chai Corner now stays open from
six in the morning to ten at night.

2
00:00:04,831 --> 00:00:06,821
Ravi cannot be there all day.

3
00:00:06,821 --> 00:00:08,261
So who decides what?

4
00:00:08,811 --> 00:00:11,773
One morning, Asha changes
the price of chai.

5
00:00:12,073 --> 00:00:14,411
That evening, Kabir changes it back.

6
00:00:14,711 --> 00:00:18,614
Customers are confused, and
nobody knows who is in charge.

7
00:00:19,264 --> 00:00:20,813
Someone must decide.

8
00:00:20,813 --> 00:00:22,146
Someone must do.

9
00:00:22,846 --> 00:00:26,267
That is the difference between
administration and management.

10
00:00:26,567 --> 00:00:29,943
Administration decides the
policies and the goals.

11
00:00:29,943 --> 00:00:32,019
It is the thinking function.

12
00:00:32,369 --> 00:00:34,721
Management carries those policies out.

13
00:00:34,721 --> 00:00:36,449
It is the doing function.

14
00:00:36,799 --> 00:00:41,369
A British writer, Oliver Sheldon, drew
this line back in nineteen twenty-three.

15
00:00:41,969 --> 00:00:46,612
By the way, a policy is just a rule
that guides everyday decisions.

16
00:00:46,962 --> 00:00:51,760
Like, one cup of chai costs fifteen
rupees, and the stall opens at six.

17
00:00:52,410 --> 00:00:54,447
So Ravi splits the work in two.

18
00:00:54,747 --> 00:00:56,518
Ravi is the administrator.

19
00:00:56,518 --> 00:00:59,821
He sets the prices, the
timings, and the goals.

20
00:01:00,171 --> 00:01:02,248
Meena becomes the shift manager.

21
00:01:02,248 --> 00:01:05,282
She runs the stall every
day, by those rules.

22
00:01:05,932 --> 00:01:08,174
Let's compare the two, row by row.

23
00:01:08,574 --> 00:01:09,474
Level.

24
00:01:09,174 --> 00:01:11,240
Administration sits at the top.

25
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:14,320
Management works at the
middle and lower levels.

26
00:01:14,670 --> 00:01:15,570
Function.

27
00:01:15,527 --> 00:01:17,186
Administration thinks.

28
00:01:17,186 --> 00:01:18,507
Management does.

29
00:01:18,857 --> 00:01:19,757
Focus.

30
00:01:19,532 --> 00:01:21,733
Administration sets the goals.

31
00:01:21,733 --> 00:01:23,536
Management reaches them.

32
00:01:23,886 --> 00:01:24,786
Decisions.

33
00:01:24,737 --> 00:01:27,100
Administration makes the big ones.

34
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:29,358
Management makes the daily ones.

35
00:01:29,708 --> 00:01:30,608
Who.

36
00:01:30,279 --> 00:01:33,078
Owners and directors do administration.

37
00:01:33,078 --> 00:01:35,877
Managers and supervisors do management.

38
00:01:36,527 --> 00:01:38,485
But experts do not all agree.

39
00:01:38,485 --> 00:01:39,996
There are three views.

40
00:01:40,396 --> 00:01:43,894
Oliver Sheldon said administration
sits above management.

41
00:01:44,244 --> 00:01:45,144
E.F.L.

42
00:01:44,785 --> 00:01:49,526
Brech said management is the bigger
idea, and administration is one part

43
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:50,426
of it.

44
00:01:50,587 --> 00:01:54,856
And many modern writers, like Harold
Koontz, use both words for the same

45
00:01:54,856 --> 00:01:55,756
thing.

46
00:01:56,068 --> 00:01:57,100
Quick check.

47
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:59,016
Four jobs at Chai Corner.

48
00:01:59,016 --> 00:02:01,027
Which one is administration?

49
00:02:02,927 --> 00:02:04,015
Setting prices!

50
00:02:04,015 --> 00:02:06,871
It is a policy decision, made at the top.

51
00:02:07,471 --> 00:02:08,480
So, remember.

52
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:11,228
Administration decides the policies.

53
00:02:11,228 --> 00:02:13,312
It is the thinking function.

54
00:02:13,662 --> 00:02:15,489
Management carries them out.

55
00:02:15,489 --> 00:02:17,229
It is the doing function.

56
00:02:17,579 --> 00:02:20,665
And there are three views:
above, inside, or the same.

57
00:02:21,265 --> 00:02:25,511
Next time, we'll climb the levels of
management, from the very top to the

58
00:02:25,511 --> 00:02:26,411
front line.
